  "scope": "Current physical validity derives captured and returned payload bounds in arbitrary populated native tables. Literal checked edge, row, and union assemblers derive constructor payload and allocation bounds from actual ordered prefixes. Original operands derive exact emitted Work width checks. A certified checked prefix has numeric causal store and constructor bounds from its original computed source mass and step count; domains use at most one identity per instruction. The complete source compiler must still produce all reached width certificates and a complete-query step bound. Whole generated-query resources, general constrained completion, convergence, concrete capacity, frontend/runtime adapters, and complete public Haskell correspondence remain open."
